    {
      "id": "LbgipU41JjS0plRJbWHcp",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3677.1784012180715,
      "y": 3443.2577965526775,
      "width": 1146.6467409685595,
      "height": 867.0692059261769,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b72",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1950575292,
      "version": 936,
      "versionNonce": 778818364,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1745258868558,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "There are 2 ways to create geospatial indexes ->\n\nQuad trees: Stores data in tree format. Each node has k children,\nfrequent updates are inefficient because requires rebalancing of the\ntree\n\nGeohashing : A base32 string is generated against each latitude and\nlongitude. Frequent updates are possible because geohashes is stored\nin sorted set data structure which performs operations in logn time.\nPlus redis is in-memory. Ideal for frequent delivery partner\nlocation update.\n\nlat - 1, long - 2\nbase32: trk4drtq\nuse prefix of above string to shard\nDense areas: Use shorter prefix to increase number of shards\nSparse areas: Use longer prefix to decrase number of shards\n\n\nES and Redis -> Geohashing\nPostGIS -> Quad trees",
      "fontSize": 33.03120784480674,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "There are 2 ways to create geospatial indexes ->\n\nQuad trees: Stores data in tree format. Each node has k children, frequent updates are inefficient because requires rebalancing of the tree\n\nGeohashing : A base32 string is generated against each latitude and longitude. Frequent updates are possible because geohashes is stored in sorted set data structure which performs operations in logn time. Plus redis is in-memory. Ideal for frequent delivery partner\nlocation update.\n\nlat - 1, long - 2\nbase32: trk4drtq\nuse prefix of above string to shard\nDense areas: Use shorter prefix to increase number of shards\nSparse areas: Use longer prefix to decrase number of shards\n\n\nES and Redis -> Geohashing\nPostGIS -> Quad trees",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "5WkxMrt3JlJt7m6IN3MA8",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1574.2899129671184,
      "y": 3097.205218572526,
      "width": 1678.17578125,
      "height": 1890,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b74",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 595586446,
      "version": 1595,
      "versionNonce": 640807630,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1745258572182,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "To handle double booking:\n\nScenario 1 (happy):\n\n1. Order service receives order confirmation\n2. Order service acquires a pessimistic lock by calling the warehouse service\n3. The warehouse service maintains 2 data\n\nstock:productId:warehouseId {\n total: 100,\n reserved: 59\n} -> total - reserved is actual quantity all the time\n\nreservation:orderId {\n quantity: 100,\n productId,\n warehouseId\n} EXPIRE 5s\n\n4. Order service creates a reservation and updates the stock (reserved key increments)\n5. Order service calls the payment service for confirmation\n6. On confirmation, reservation key is deleted, stock total is decremented and reserved is also \ndecremented\n\n\nScenario 2:\n\nPayment fails immediately:\n\n-> Order service receives a callback \n-> Order service deletes the reservation key, decreases the reserved count\n\n\nScenario 3:\nOrder service takes more than 5s:\n\n-> The reservation key expires\n-> An event is sent to the warehouse service\n-> The warehouse service decrements the reserved count\n\nThis also takes care of scenarios where order service crashes\n",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "To handle double booking:\n\nScenario 1 (happy):\n\n1. Order service receives order confirmation\n2. Order service acquires a pessimistic lock by calling the warehouse service\n3. The warehouse service maintains 2 data\n\nstock:productId:warehouseId {\n total: 100,\n reserved: 59\n} -> total - reserved is actual quantity all the time\n\nreservation:orderId {\n quantity: 100,\n productId,\n warehouseId\n} EXPIRE 5s\n\n4. Order service creates a reservation and updates the stock (reserved key increments)\n5. Order service calls the payment service for confirmation\n6. On confirmation, reservation key is deleted, stock total is decremented and reserved is also \ndecremented\n\n\nScenario 2:\n\nPayment fails immediately:\n\n-> Order service receives a callback \n-> Order service deletes the reservation key, decreases the reserved count\n\n\nScenario 3:\nOrder service takes more than 5s:\n\n-> The reservation key expires\n-> An event is sent to the warehouse service\n-> The warehouse service decrements the reserved count\n\nThis also takes care of scenarios where order service crashes\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
  ],
